::slack::admin ns
meta {
    doc: """
    Slack Admin API (`admin.*`) bindings for Enterprise organizations:
    conversations, workspaces (teams), users and sessions, apps, emoji,
    invite requests, IDP groups, roles, information barriers, auth
    policies, analytics, workflows and functions. One module per area,
    under `::slack::admin::*`.

    **Setup**: set `slack.admin.token` to a user token (`xoxp-...`) from an
    app installed on the whole Enterprise organization by an Org Owner or
    Org Admin, with the `admin.*` scopes the calls need. Bot tokens and
    workspace-level installs are rejected by every admin method.

    Every call returns Slack's response body. Slack answers HTTP 200 with
    `ok: false` for failures; those come back as an `Err(SlackError)`
    carrying Slack's `error` code and `response_metadata.messages`.

    **Quick start**

    ```hot
    ::users ::slack::admin::users
    ::conversations ::slack::admin::conversations

    stale ::conversations/lookup-all(::conversations/LookupRequest({
      team_ids: ["T0123ABCDEF"],
      last_message_activity_before: 1735689600
    }), 500)
    ::conversations/bulk-archive(::conversations/BulkArchiveRequest({channel_ids: slice(stale, 0, 100)}))

    ::users/session-reset(::users/SessionResetRequest({user_id: "U0123ABCDEF"}))
    ```
    """
}
